las","/farmland-atlas/oklahoma/garfield-county"],["ARC or PLC in Garfield County","/arc-plc/oklahoma/garfield-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years. In 2025 that same pair ran 27% of normal on the middle, after January to February came in at 41% in 2025. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 27% of normal on the middle. Grid 19629 had its driest year in 1956 at 43%.</p>"}
